": "the analysis did not use two-way clustering, due to computational limitations", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["two-way clustering"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [116]}, {"id": 118, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[110, 110]], "assertion": "a mixed-effects model with player random intercepts was run as an alternative to the clustered logistic regression", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["mixed effects model"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [119]}, {"id": 119, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[110, 110]], "assertion": "the mixed-effects alternative yielded similar results, though these results were not shown", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["mixed effects model results"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [118]}, {"id": 120, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[111, 111]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 121, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[112, 112]], "note": "Software subheading"}, {"id": 122, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[113, 113]], "assertion": "the analysis used Python 3.11", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["software"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 123, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[114, 114]], "assertion": "the analysis used statsmodels 0.14 (GLM with cluster-robust covariance)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["software"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 124, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[115, 115]], "assertion": "the bootstrap was implemented manually using numpy random sampling", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["bootstrap implementation"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 125, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[116, 116]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 126, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[117, 117]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 127, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[118, 118]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 128, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [